event_log: extract timestamp token before dateStringToEpoch

getUniqueEntryID() was passing the full log line to dateStringToEpoch().
dateStringToEpoch() rejects any input that has characters remaining after
the parsed timestamp, so entries in the format
"<timestamp> <MessageId>,<args>" failed before they could be dispatched to
EventService subscribers.

Extract only the timestamp token before calling dateStringToEpoch().

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: HTTPS-Guard <https-guard@openbmc>

--- a/redfish-core/src/event_log.cpp
+++ b/redfish-core/src/event_log.cpp
@@ -32,8 +32,15 @@ bool getUniqueEntryID(UniqueEntryIDState& state, const std::string& logEntry,
                       std::string& entryID)
 {
     // Get the entry timestamp
+    // The log line format is "<Timestamp> <MessageId>,<MessageArgs>".
+    // dateStringToEpoch() rejects strings with trailing content, so extract
+    // only the timestamp token (first space-delimited field).
+    size_t space = logEntry.find_first_of(' ');
+    std::string_view tsStr = (space != std::string::npos)
+                                 ? std::string_view(logEntry).substr(0, space)
+                                 : std::string_view(logEntry);
     std::optional<time_utils::usSinceEpoch> curTs =
-        time_utils::dateStringToEpoch(logEntry);
+        time_utils::dateStringToEpoch(tsStr);
     if (!curTs)
     {
         return false;
